course: dictionary
lesson: 10456
title: Truthful and honest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Truthful means telling the truth, so it is not lying. You can meet it at school, at home and in stories. «Please tell me truthfully what happened» asks for an honest answer, with nothing hidden. Here truthfully is the adverb form of truthful.
explain: In a story, a truthful character can be trusted. Alice, «a very truthful child», admits she has tasted eggs, even when the Pigeon thinks she might be a serpent. The word tells you what kind of person she is, so you can see why readers trust her.
explain: Truthful has a second meaning too: true, giving a correct picture of what happened. «Her truthful account of the accident helped the police.» An account is a report, so here truthful means accurate. Check any meaning by swapping in honest or true and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Truthful means telling the truth; honest, not lying.
fact: A truthful account is a report that gives a correct picture of what happened.
fact: Christians believe God is truthful and cannot lie (Titus 1:2).
fact: Proverbs 12:19 says, «Truthful lips endure for ever, but a lying tongue lasts only a moment.»
fact: Aristotle said the truthful person stands in the middle: the boaster claims more than is true, and the falsely modest claims less.
exercise: «Please tell me truthfully what happened.» What does truthfully mean here? | *Honestly, without hiding anything | Loudly, so everyone can hear | Secretly, behind a closed door | Quickly, in a hurry
exercise: «Her truthful account of the accident helped the police.» What does truthful mean here? | *Giving a correct picture of what happened | Very long and boring | Told in a whisper | Full of jokes
exercise: Alice is called «a very truthful child». Why? | Because she is the tallest in the class | Because she is always asleep | *Because she tells the truth, even about something odd | Because she never speaks at all
test: A truthful answer means the same as which? | Quiet answer | *Honest answer | Lazy answer | Long answer
test: «Christians believe God is truthful.» What does this mean? | *God always tells the truth and cannot lie | God is always busy | God is always late | God lives in a castle
exam: You broke the vase by accident and your mum asks what happened. Which answer is truthful? | It was a dragon | I have no idea what you mean | No, I have never been in the kitchen | *Yes, I broke it by accident, and I am sorry
